libnfs, the NFS client library by Ronnie Sahlberg and contributors
https://github.com/sahlberg/libnfs, commit 7613236464317bee2d9636f087f995148de4db27

Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later for lib/ and include/ (COPYING, LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt);
the protocol definitions (*.x) and the files generated from them
(*/libnfs-raw-*.[ch]) BSD-2-Clause (LICENCE-BSD.txt).
Only the client library is here: lib/ (without Kerberos), include/, and the
mount, nfs, nfs4 and portmap protocols. NLM, NSM, rquota, the examples,
utilities, servers and tests are left out.

Porpoise reads games on an NFS share with it (src/porpoise_netfs.cpp).
tools/build.sh compiles each file in sources.txt as C with ps5/config.h.

Changes from upstream:
- ps5/config.h: the configuration for the PS5's FreeBSD headers (upstream
  makes config.h with CMake or autoconf). No HAVE_SIGNAL_H, so the library
  doesn't set SIGPIPE to ignored for the whole app.
- lib/socket.c: on the PS5, the console's own SO_NBIO makes a socket
  non-blocking (fcntl's O_NONBLOCK doesn't take there), with read and write
  time limits and SO_NOSIGPIPE; and a reconnect closes the old socket
  instead of dup2() onto it (as on Windows), so there's no dup2 import
  (Porpoise turns the library's own reconnecting off and reconnects itself).
- include/nfsc/libnfs-raw-mount.h: a copy of mount/libnfs-raw-mount.h, where
  upstream installs it, for Porpoise to include.
- The build renames getaddrinfo, freeaddrinfo, getprotobyname, getservbyport
  and getnameinfo to src/porpoise_netfs.cpp's (the console's libc has none of
  them in the modules Porpoise loads), and defines NDEBUG.
